    "narrative": "LawDog enters the July 4th slate with a focus on exploiting soft pitching matchups to drive volume in our counting categories. **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) stands as our premier play today; he benefits significantly from a favorable park environment and a middle-of-the-order spot against a pitcher in Alcantara whose efficiency has dipped, making him a prime candidate to anchor our offensive output. **Tyler Freeman** (72.83) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) are also high-leverage starts, both bolstered by a significant boost from facing the southpaw Sullivan in a hitter-friendly park. While **Luis Arraez** loses points for the platoon disadvantage, his contact profile against the high-xERA Sullivan remains a statistical outlier we are happy to leverage for batting average stability.\n\nWe are closely monitoring **Bryson Stott** (64.54), who holds a strong efficiency score but carries a 40% rain risk; he remains a start due to his elite ability to contribute to our scarcity-driven stolen base targets, despite the threat of a washout. In contrast, **Yainer Diaz** (40.31) and **Daulton Varsho** (47.69) represent our most marginal starters. **Yainer Diaz** is essentially at the floor due to a tough matchup against Rasmussen, but his lack of high-ceiling alternatives forces him into the slot. **Taylor Ward** (41.87) was the most difficult exclusion from our starting nine; he was bypassed primarily because his projected efficiency against Greene failed to outpace the structural advantages provided by the platoon and order positions of our currently rostered outfielders. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are relying on the depth provided by **Gavin Sheets** and **Masyn Winn** to bridge the gap, though both face steep challenges against Yamamoto and Imanaga, respectively.",
